     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the typical maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney function.\n\nCould you check what was intended? Some possibilities:\n- **1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), which is the max dose.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg three times daily**, or another standard regimen.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I can add a note to the order. Pharmacy will probably flag it."
      }
